configure.ac, setup.py: allow cross builds for Haiku

configure refuses a cross build for a host it does not name in its _host_cpu cases (the
_PYTHON_HOST_PLATFORM suffix): HaikuPorts' patchset adds Haiku to the MACHDEP list but not to this
one. With it, _PYTHON_HOST_PLATFORM is haiku-aarch64, and setup.py (which 3.10 still uses for the
extension modules) has to match "haiku" as a prefix, not the whole platform name, to take its
Haiku paths and skip nis.

HaikuPorts builds natively and never takes this path. Applied after HaikuPorts'
python3.10-3.10.22.patchset by scripts/build-python.sh --version 3.10.22, which regenerates
configure with autoconf.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -456,6 +456,9 @@
 	*-*-vxworks*)
 		_host_cpu=$host_cpu
 		;;
+	*-*-haiku*)
+		_host_cpu=$host_cpu
+		;;
 	*)
 		# for now, limit cross builds to known configurations
 		MACHDEP="unknown"
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@
 MACOS = (HOST_PLATFORM == 'darwin')
 AIX = (HOST_PLATFORM.startswith('aix'))
 VXWORKS = ('vxworks' in HOST_PLATFORM)
-HAIKU = (HOST_PLATFORM == 'haiku')
+HAIKU = HOST_PLATFORM.startswith('haiku')
 CC = os.environ.get("CC")
 if not CC:
     CC = sysconfig.get_config_var("CC")
